    {
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 1060,
        "content": "## Recording link (Dropbox or presigned URL) to transcript Google Doc - large files, safe retries\n\n**Who it's for:** teams whose recordings live in Dropbox, S3, R2, Google Cloud Storage, Azure or any storage that can hand out a link, and who want a transcript Google Doc without downloading 200-500 MB videos into n8n.\n\n### How it works\n1. Send `POST /webhook/transcribe-recording-link` with JSON: `{\"url\": \"<presigned URL>\", \"fileName\": \"meeting.mp4\"}` or `{\"dropboxPath\": \"/Recordings/meeting.mp4\"}` (the flow asks Dropbox for a temporary link itself). Optional: `sourceFileId` (your own id).\n2. **Source file id**: your id, else the Dropbox file id, else the presigned URL without its signature. It stays the same for every new link to the same file.\n3. If a Doc for this source id is already **complete**, the flow stops: no new Apify run, no second Doc.\n4. **tidytools/audio-transcriber** downloads the file itself (streamed to disk, up to 2 GB, interrupted downloads continue) and returns the transcript.\n5. A Google Doc tagged with the source id is created (or the one an earlier failed try started is reused), the text is written, and the Doc is marked complete.\n\n### Retries never pay twice\n`resumeStore` keeps finished transcripts by source file id. If the execution fails after the transcript was made, retry it: the saved transcript is returned (not charged) and the half-made Doc is reused.\n\n### Cost (Apify pay-per-event, October 2026)\n$0.006 per audio minute (60 minutes = $0.36). Failed downloads, files without speech and reused transcripts are free. The Apify node caps each run at $3.\n\n### Setup (5 minutes)\nCredentials: Apify API, Google Drive OAuth2, and Dropbox OAuth2 only for `dropboxPath`. Presigned URLs should stay valid for at least 2 hours. Adjust **Transcript settings**; **Test with an example** runs a short sample file."
      },
